# The student's main block calls four functions in a row that take and give nothing: the frame travels beside the
# route, through the module's `df`, a place the steps write and read. `get_data` downloads on every run and reads the
# raw file back itself, so the file is what it leaves behind, in the codomain; `plot` draws on pyplot's own figure.

route sunspots
step sunspots/get_data
step sunspots/get_data/get                                        # `r = requests.get(url)`
step sunspots/get_data/open                                       # `with open(..) as f`
step sunspots/get_data/read_csv                                   # `df = pd.read_csv(..)`
step sunspots/clean
step sunspots/clean/drop                                          # `df.drop(.., inplace=True)` changes the frame
step sunspots/clean/reset_index                                   # `df.reset_index(drop=True, inplace=True)`
step sunspots/smooth
step sunspots/plot

line entry > sunspots call
line Web(www.sidc.be) > sunspots/get_data own
line sunspots/get_data/get > Response·r@sunspots/get_data/get value
known #101 line Response·r@sunspots/get_data/get > sunspots/get_data value          # `f.write(r.text)`
line sunspots/get_data/open > TextIOWrapper·f@sunspots/get_data/open value
known #101 line TextIOWrapper·f@sunspots/get_data/open > sunspots/get_data value   # `f.write(r.text)`
line sunspots/get_data > File(data/raw/sunspots.csv) own          # and reads it back in its own body
line sunspots/get_data/read_csv > DataFrame·df@sunspots/get_data/read_csv value
known #101 line DataFrame·df@sunspots/get_data/read_csv > sunspots/get_data value   # kept in the module's `df`
line sunspots/get_data > Global(sunspots.df) own
line Global(sunspots.df) > sunspots/clean own                     # what `drop` runs on is the module's `df`
line sunspots/clean/drop > DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/drop value
line DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/drop > sunspots/clean/reset_index value
line sunspots/clean/reset_index > DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/reset_index value
known #101 line DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/reset_index > sunspots/clean value       # it stays in the module's `df`
line sunspots/clean > Global(sunspots.df) own
line Global(sunspots.df) > sunspots/smooth own
line sunspots/smooth > Global(sunspots.df) own
line Global(sunspots.df) > sunspots/plot own
line sunspots/plot > Figure own                                # pyplot's current figure, `plt.figure(..)`
line sunspots/plot > File(figures/sunspots.png) own

home Response·r@sunspots/get_data/get sunspots/get_data
home TextIOWrapper·f@sunspots/get_data/open sunspots/get_data
home DataFrame·df@sunspots/get_data/read_csv sunspots/get_data
home DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/drop sunspots/clean
home DataFrame·df@sunspots/clean/reset_index sunspots/clean

side entry left
side Web(www.sidc.be) left
side File(data/raw/sunspots.csv) right
side Global(sunspots.df) between
side Figure right
side File(figures/sunspots.png) right

# a library call whose result no name holds is drawn as a step: what it gives should go into the call around it
